From 3d4f8629ff5f7ddf38c16ab97a928dcea9020ada Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gili Tzabari <cowwoc2020@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 22:07:55 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Build with Rust 1.99.1 so macOS links pass under fatal linker
 messages

Rust 1.95 reports ld's "ignoring duplicate libraries: '-lSystem'" through
linker_messages, which the workspace denies. libSystem is linked by both std
and block2 (via os_info's objc2-foundation), so every macOS link of
codex-code-mode-host fails. Since Rust 1.96 rustc files that message, and
ld's "built for newer macOS version" notes, under the allow-by-default
linker_info lint.

Pin Rust 1.99.1, the latest stable release, in rust-toolchain.toml, the
Bazel toolchain, setup-windows.ps1 and every workflow's toolchain action.
